1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,253
[TALIA] <i>Well, your plan worked.</i>

2
00:00:03,878 --> 00:00:05,755
<i>Because of you, Ms. Talia.</i>

3
00:00:06,339 --> 00:00:08,925
[BILLY] <i>There's only one thing</i>
<i>you need to know, Ms. Talia.</i>

4
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:12,554
<i>You can't trust Bea Mercado.</i>

5
00:00:13,138 --> 00:00:15,056
<i>We hit the jackpot with this!</i>

6
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:16,683
<i>But more importantly,</i>

7
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:19,477
<i>it will be a big blow to Billy.</i>

8
00:00:19,561 --> 00:00:22,564
<i>Good thing she took the bait.</i>

9
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:24,149
<i>Thank you.</i>

10
00:00:24,232 --> 00:00:26,109
<i>Billy, anything for you.</i>

11
00:00:26,192 --> 00:00:29,487
<i>I can't believe she didn't involve us</i>
<i>in the plan.</i>

12
00:00:29,571 --> 00:00:33,575
<i>It would have been risky</i>
<i>if she'd told us the plan, right?</i>

13
00:00:33,658 --> 00:00:35,785
<i>But still, it's a shame, isn't it?</i>

14
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:37,871
<i>I mean, imagine the suspense</i>

15
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:40,790
<i>and the contents we could have</i>
<i>made out of it, right?</i>

16
00:00:41,791 --> 00:00:47,464
[JORDAN] <i>♪ Even in the silence ♪</i>

17
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:53,428
<i>♪ You're the only one</i>
<i>On my mind ♪</i>

18
00:00:54,179 --> 00:00:56,890
<i>♪ Can we take a rest? ♪</i>

19
00:00:57,515 --> 00:01:00,810
<i>♪ I might say something I'll regret ♪</i>

20
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:05,607
<i>♪ Baby, I won't be long ♪</i>

21
00:01:06,357 --> 00:01:09,903
<i>♪ I'll be back by the end of the song ♪</i>

22
00:01:09,986 --> 00:01:11,071
[BEA] <i>Please.</i>

23
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,907
<i>Please, I'm begging you.</i>

24
00:01:14,574 --> 00:01:17,202
<i>Do you know I'm getting</i>
<i>in trouble because of you?</i>

25
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:18,369
<i>Just leave me alone.</i>

26
00:01:18,453 --> 00:01:21,873
<i>Because they think we're accomplices.</i>

27
00:01:23,124 --> 00:01:25,084
<i>I could even go to jail because of you.</i>

28
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:26,795
<i>So please, I'm begging you.</i>

29
00:01:27,337 --> 00:01:30,423
<i>Please, please. Stay away from me.</i>

30
00:01:32,008 --> 00:01:34,803
[LAUGHING]

31
00:01:34,886 --> 00:01:37,722
<i>Accomplices?! You got that right!</i>
<i>We're accomplices!</i>

32
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:39,057
<i>Accomplices in love, right?</i>

33
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:41,601
<i>- Crazy! You're crazy!</i>
- [CALOY] <i>That's how, right?</i>

34
00:01:41,684 --> 00:01:42,811
[BEA] <i>Ma'am, you see?</i>

35
00:01:42,894 --> 00:01:44,854
<i>I had nothing to do with him!</i>

36
00:01:45,730 --> 00:01:47,273
<i>He's totally out of his mind.</i>

37
00:01:47,357 --> 00:01:50,652
<i>I never asked him to do anything</i>
<i>because I don't even know him!</i>

38
00:01:50,735 --> 00:01:53,071
[EVENT MC] <i>Please join me as we celebrate</i>

39
00:01:53,154 --> 00:01:56,866
<i>one of today's</i>
<i>Young Entrepreneurial awardees,</i>

40
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:59,661
<i>Ms. Benilda Cariño.</i>

41
00:02:04,749 --> 00:02:06,417
[BILLY] <i>A few years ago,</i>

42
00:02:06,501 --> 00:02:09,546
<i>my friends and I were just talking about</i>

43
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:11,131
<i>love.</i>

44
00:02:11,214 --> 00:02:15,135
<i>And from those honest</i>
<i>late-night conversations,</i>

45
00:02:15,844 --> 00:02:17,679
<i>LoveList was born.</i>

46
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:21,141
<i>LoveList stands where it is today</i>

47
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:23,434
<i>because of my team,</i>

48
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:25,562
<i>my best friend,</i>

49
00:02:25,645 --> 00:02:27,480
<i>my LoveList family,</i>

50
00:02:28,398 --> 00:02:29,983
<i>and my family.</i>

51
00:02:30,066 --> 00:02:33,903
<i>I promise, from here on,</i>
<i>it only gets better.</i>

52
00:02:33,987 --> 00:02:37,532
<i>Because every Filipina</i>
<i>deserves to feel safe</i>

53
00:02:37,615 --> 00:02:39,742
<i>and empowered in love.</i>

54
00:02:39,826 --> 00:02:42,412
<i>Again, thank you very much.</i>

55
00:02:42,996 --> 00:02:47,333
[APPLAUSE]

56
00:02:49,043 --> 00:02:52,922
Dude, cheers to you
and to your genius plan.

57
00:02:53,006 --> 00:02:54,132
Genius!

58
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:55,466
Congrats to us.

59
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:56,843
- Thank you.
- [JORDAN] And now…

60
00:02:57,594 --> 00:03:00,471
Caloy's behind bars.

61
00:03:00,555 --> 00:03:01,931
One problem solved.

62
00:03:02,015 --> 00:03:03,391
Cheers!

63
00:03:03,474 --> 00:03:07,770
And cheers to your acting too!
Because you're the best actor.

64
00:03:07,854 --> 00:03:10,899
You really nailed it earlier.

65
00:03:10,982 --> 00:03:12,692
Of course. You know how talented I am.

66
00:03:12,775 --> 00:03:14,944
Mm! You really are!

67
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:15,987
Did you see earlier?

68
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:19,324
After your performance,
so many women came up to you.

69
00:03:19,407 --> 00:03:21,200
They were handing you their calling cards.

70
00:03:21,284 --> 00:03:23,620
I don't know if those were offers
for gigs or dates.

71
00:03:23,703 --> 00:03:24,662
Which were they?

72
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:27,206
Both. Duh!

73
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:30,919
Wow, you really are so talented!

74
00:03:31,002 --> 00:03:32,420
- Cheers to that.
- [BOTTLES CLINK]

75
00:03:32,503 --> 00:03:34,047
[BILLY CHUCKLES]

76
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:36,466
[WOMAN SINGING IN BACKGROUND]

77
00:03:36,549 --> 00:03:40,720
[PEOPLE APPLAUDING]

78
00:03:40,803 --> 00:03:42,138
Oh, it's your turn. Do you want to--

79
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:43,389
You should perform.

80
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:45,225
- Let's both do it.
- They're done.

81
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:46,309
Wanna do it?

82
00:03:46,809 --> 00:03:48,269
Thank you.

83
00:03:48,353 --> 00:03:50,521
[PEOPLE APPLAUDING]

84
00:03:52,273 --> 00:03:57,612
["ABELYANA" BY MAKI PLAYING]

85
00:04:09,332 --> 00:04:11,459
So annoying. I said I don't feel like it!

86
00:04:15,213 --> 00:04:21,052
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

87
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:42,991
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

88
00:04:58,965 --> 00:05:05,388
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

89
00:05:20,778 --> 00:05:27,243
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

90
00:05:42,925 --> 00:05:46,846
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

91
00:06:04,947 --> 00:06:11,287
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

92
00:06:26,969 --> 00:06:33,184
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

93
00:06:48,908 --> 00:06:54,914
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

94
00:07:10,972 --> 00:07:16,519
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

95
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:32,452
[MUSIC ENDS]

96
00:07:38,082 --> 00:07:44,422
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

97
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:05,693
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

98
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:17,163
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

99
00:09:07,505 --> 00:09:09,590
- Oh. Billy.
- Hi, Auntie Pres.

100
00:09:09,674 --> 00:09:11,217
- You came home?
- Mm-hmm.

101
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:14,929
Why didn't you just stay
at the hotel overnight?

102
00:09:15,012 --> 00:09:16,597
- What a waste.
- No, it's fine.

103
00:09:16,681 --> 00:09:18,724
You could've just
spent time with your friends.

104
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:20,101
[BILLY] It's okay.

105
00:09:20,685 --> 00:09:24,063
With the amount of stress
you're dealing with,

106
00:09:24,146 --> 00:09:26,857
you deserve to let off some steam
and have fun.

107
00:09:27,441 --> 00:09:28,568
You know, Auntie Pres,

108
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:32,655
my real stress-relievers
are you and Oliver.

109
00:09:32,738 --> 00:09:37,201
Knowing that you're both safe
makes me happy.

110
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:41,080
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

111
00:09:41,163 --> 00:09:42,498
Good night.

112
00:09:42,582 --> 00:09:44,125
- Good night.
- Huh?

113
00:09:44,875 --> 00:09:46,127
Go to sleep, please.

114
00:09:46,210 --> 00:09:47,795
[PRECIOUS CHUCKLES]

115
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:55,678
- [MUSIC FADES]
- [ENRICO SIGHS]

116
00:10:01,559 --> 00:10:02,560
Enrico.

117
00:10:02,643 --> 00:10:06,022
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

118
00:10:06,105 --> 00:10:07,356
Well?

119
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:10,735
It's way past your 10-day deadline
with Boss Zandro.

120
00:10:10,818 --> 00:10:12,069
Where's the payment?

121
00:10:12,153 --> 00:10:15,656
I've sent Zandro 20,000 pesos.

122
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:17,742
Twenty thousand pesos?

123
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:18,868
Are you stupid?

124
00:10:18,951 --> 00:10:21,662
You owe him 20,000 dollars.

125
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:24,373
I'll pay in full

126
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:25,750
next month.

127
00:10:26,542 --> 00:10:28,711
Do you think I'm an idiot? Huh?

128
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:33,299
You think I was just bluffing
with my threat?

129
00:10:33,924 --> 00:10:35,926
[BOTH GRUNTING]

130
00:10:37,928 --> 00:10:39,096
[BLOW LANDS]

131
00:10:39,930 --> 00:10:41,682
- [GRUNTS]
- [BLOWS LAND]

132
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:42,892
[THUG GROANS]

133
00:10:42,975 --> 00:10:49,940
- [PANTING]
- [TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

134
00:10:53,444 --> 00:10:54,987
[PANICKED SHOUTS]

135
00:10:55,071 --> 00:10:56,072
Help!

136
00:10:56,155 --> 00:10:58,324
Let's take him to the hospital!

137
00:10:58,407 --> 00:10:59,700
Sir, are you okay?

138
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:07,291
Oliver, put that away, please.
It's mealtime.

139
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:08,626
Okay.

140
00:11:08,709 --> 00:11:10,169
Who are you chatting with?

141
00:11:10,252 --> 00:11:11,671
Biboy.

142
00:11:11,754 --> 00:11:14,840
He's asking to come with me
and Suzie to study.

143
00:11:14,924 --> 00:11:16,509
Oh, really?

144
00:11:16,592 --> 00:11:17,510
You've made up?

145
00:11:17,593 --> 00:11:19,804
Mm-hmm. Sir Eric made them
patch things up.

146
00:11:19,887 --> 00:11:21,138
- [BAG ZIPS]
- Hmm.

147
00:11:21,222 --> 00:11:23,099
He's become nicer to me.

148
00:11:23,182 --> 00:11:26,018
Has he really?
Or is he just scared of Sir Eric?

149
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:27,144
Mm!

150
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:28,687
But that's good.

151
00:11:28,771 --> 00:11:31,482
I should give my thanks to that Sir Eric.

152
00:11:31,565 --> 00:11:34,360
Mm-hmm. That's right. You really should.

153
00:11:34,443 --> 00:11:37,154
He's such a nice guy, if you meet him.

154
00:11:37,238 --> 00:11:38,906
- Auntie Pres…
- It's true.

155
00:11:38,989 --> 00:11:41,534
What if you go there today to meet him?

156
00:11:41,617 --> 00:11:42,660
Today?

157
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:46,247
Oh, I can't. I have a breakfast meeting.

158
00:11:46,330 --> 00:11:48,541
Sorry. I'll try to go at lunchtime.

159
00:11:48,624 --> 00:11:50,418
- Are you sure?
- Yes. I'll try.

160
00:11:50,501 --> 00:11:53,254
- I'll hold you to that.
- Yes.

161
00:11:53,337 --> 00:11:54,255
[PRECIOUS] Okay.

162
00:11:54,338 --> 00:11:57,091
Oliver, can you stop chatting
during meals, please?

163
00:11:57,174 --> 00:11:59,552
- Put that away.
- Mm!

164
00:11:59,635 --> 00:12:02,721
And finish your breakfast.
I'm taking you to school.

165
00:12:02,805 --> 00:12:05,641
But don't worry,
this will be the last time.

166
00:12:05,724 --> 00:12:07,351
You won't have a chaperone
starting next week.

167
00:12:07,435 --> 00:12:08,853
But it's okay.

168
00:12:08,936 --> 00:12:11,021
It's fine that you're always at school.

169
00:12:11,105 --> 00:12:12,982
I'm an Auntie's boy anyway,

170
00:12:13,065 --> 00:12:14,900
and a Billy's boy.

171
00:12:14,984 --> 00:12:16,694
- What a flatterer.
- That won't work on us.

172
00:12:16,777 --> 00:12:19,155
- We know you'd love that.
- You're smooth-talking us.

173
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:21,365
- Okay, enough with that.
- Turn it off.

174
00:12:21,449 --> 00:12:22,366
I'll take this.

175
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:24,076
- [PRECIOUS] Enough.
- Keep eating now.

176
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:26,537
I'll pack your lunch.

177
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:28,873
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

178
00:12:28,956 --> 00:12:31,584
Okay, so for full verification,

179
00:12:31,667 --> 00:12:33,878
we'll need backend access to your system.

180
00:12:33,961 --> 00:12:36,881
It's for real-time ID check
and fraud monitoring.

181
00:12:36,964 --> 00:12:39,633
Yes, but only limited API access.

182
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:43,596
We can't grant you direct access
to our main database.

183
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:47,099
Sensitive data must be encrypted with us.

184
00:12:47,183 --> 00:12:49,059
This makes it safer for our users.

185
00:12:49,143 --> 00:12:52,271
Okay. Will it be possible to do
in eight weeks?

186
00:12:52,354 --> 00:12:53,439
Six weeks.

187
00:12:54,356 --> 00:12:57,610
We already have a framework.
We just have to do the integration.

188
00:12:58,444 --> 00:13:00,529
Very confident, Mr. Valentin.

189
00:13:01,489 --> 00:13:03,240
Confidence is preparation.

190
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:06,702
Then we have a deal.

191
00:13:06,785 --> 00:13:08,078
- Sir Andy, thank you.
- Yeah.

192
00:13:08,162 --> 00:13:09,497
Thank you. Thank you very much.

193
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:10,414
Thank you.

194
00:13:10,498 --> 00:13:11,832
Okay. Thank you. I'll go ahead.

195
00:13:11,916 --> 00:13:14,168
- Yes. We'll see you soon. Thank you.
- Take care.

196
00:13:15,294 --> 00:13:16,962
[MUSIC FADES]

197
00:13:18,172 --> 00:13:19,298
Six weeks?

198
00:13:19,381 --> 00:13:21,342
You sure about that, dude?

199
00:13:22,384 --> 00:13:26,096
You don't trust me? That's basic!

200
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:27,681
Not really. [CLICKS TONGUE]

201
00:13:27,765 --> 00:13:29,725
[CHUCKLES] Is that so?

202
00:13:29,808 --> 00:13:32,186
- Fine. Ten weeks.
- Oh, I take it back!

203
00:13:32,269 --> 00:13:34,563
Thank you. Thank you.

204
00:13:34,647 --> 00:13:36,732
Gosh, what would I do

205
00:13:36,815 --> 00:13:40,027
if I didn't have
my ridiculously cocky best friend?

206
00:13:40,110 --> 00:13:40,945
Mm!

207
00:13:41,028 --> 00:13:45,199
He's talented, handsome, and smells good!

208
00:13:45,282 --> 00:13:46,659
He's perfect!

209
00:13:46,742 --> 00:13:48,744
All he's missing is a girlfriend.

210
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:51,539
We'll find one for him. Mm!

211
00:13:51,622 --> 00:13:58,254
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

212
00:13:59,755 --> 00:14:00,839
Stop flattering me.

213
00:14:02,091 --> 00:14:04,718
I'm the only one
you'll hear that from, you know.

214
00:14:04,802 --> 00:14:06,220
By the way,

215
00:14:06,303 --> 00:14:09,098
I'm going to Oliver's school.

216
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:11,475
I want to meet that Eric guy
they always talk about

217
00:14:11,559 --> 00:14:13,060
so I can thank him.

218
00:14:14,979 --> 00:14:16,438
Okay, I'm coming with you.

219
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:18,107
- Okay.
- [PHONE RINGING]

220
00:14:20,276 --> 00:14:21,735
Here's your cake, ma'am.

221
00:14:21,819 --> 00:14:22,736
Hello? Thank you.

222
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:25,072
[WOMAN] <i>May I speak with Benilda Cariño?</i>

223
00:14:25,155 --> 00:14:26,991
Speaking. Who's this?

224
00:14:27,074 --> 00:14:30,327
<i>Ma'am, this is Nurse Anj</i>
<i>from St. John Hospital.</i>

225
00:14:30,411 --> 00:14:32,830
<i>You're listed as an emergency contact.</i>

226
00:14:33,497 --> 00:14:35,499
Emergency contact for whom?

227
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:36,458
Oliver?

228
00:14:36,542 --> 00:14:38,669
<i>For patient Enrico Dominguez.</i>

229
00:14:38,752 --> 00:14:44,592
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

230
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:47,761
[BILLY] Why?

231
00:14:49,013 --> 00:14:50,598
What happened to him?

232
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:05,738
I'll take a look first if you want.

233
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:07,823
It's okay.

234
00:15:10,492 --> 00:15:14,538
Miss, what room is Enrico Dominguez in?

235
00:15:14,622 --> 00:15:16,624
What's your relationship with the patient?

236
00:15:16,707 --> 00:15:20,294
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

237
00:15:20,377 --> 00:15:21,587
He's my father.

238
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:22,796
He's in Bed 3.

239
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:25,299
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

240
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:45,694
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

241
00:15:48,906 --> 00:15:49,949
Are you a relative?

242
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:53,160
[ECG MONITOR BEEPING]

243
00:15:57,539 --> 00:15:58,791
Yes, boss.

244
00:15:58,874 --> 00:16:00,876
Okay, I'll take care of it.

245
00:16:03,837 --> 00:16:06,674
He's still unconscious,
but his vitals are stable.

246
00:16:06,757 --> 00:16:09,927
We'll keep him under observation
for the next 24 hours.

247
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:13,180
It's important that
we monitor him closely tonight.

248
00:16:13,806 --> 00:16:14,640
Okay, Doc.

249
00:16:17,685 --> 00:16:24,566
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

250
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:28,112
So his blood sugar just dropped.

251
00:16:28,946 --> 00:16:30,030
He'll be fine.

252
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:32,366
Awesome, isn't it?

253
00:16:32,449 --> 00:16:34,952
Of all the things he could've
passed down to my brother,

254
00:16:35,035 --> 00:16:36,745
it just had to be diabetes.

255
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:43,711
Miss, how much is the bill
for Enrico Dominguez?

256
00:16:43,794 --> 00:16:45,879
- [CASHIER] One moment, ma'am.
- Thank you.

257
00:16:47,881 --> 00:16:49,216
Here, ma'am.

258
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:56,932
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

259
00:17:02,646 --> 00:17:03,647
[BILLY] What?

260
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:06,984
I thought you didn't care about your dad?

261
00:17:08,819 --> 00:17:09,653
I don't.

262
00:17:12,531 --> 00:17:18,620
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

263
00:17:21,415 --> 00:17:24,418
Auntie, I'm so excited for Billy
to finally meet Sir Eric.

264
00:17:24,501 --> 00:17:29,048
Me too. I'm sure your sister's
also going to like him.

265
00:17:29,131 --> 00:17:33,802
You too? You mean you like…?

266
00:17:33,886 --> 00:17:36,388
Hey, cut it out! It's not like that.

267
00:17:36,472 --> 00:17:38,265
I'm okay with it, Auntie.

268
00:17:38,348 --> 00:17:40,059
I think you and Sir Eric
make a better couple

269
00:17:40,142 --> 00:17:41,393
than you and Coach Brandon.

270
00:17:41,477 --> 00:17:42,728
What are you talking about?

271
00:17:42,811 --> 00:17:45,064
You're too young to be thinking
about things like that.

272
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:46,523
I didn't just come up with it.

273
00:17:46,607 --> 00:17:48,108
I see it.

274
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:51,361
You get way more excited around him
than you did with Coach Brandon.

275
00:17:51,445 --> 00:17:53,030
- What?!
- [BOTH LAUGH]

276
00:17:53,113 --> 00:17:55,282
- Oh.
- [LUCY] Hi.

277
00:17:55,365 --> 00:17:56,450
Good morning.

278
00:17:56,533 --> 00:17:58,035
Is Sir Eric here?

279
00:17:58,118 --> 00:18:01,747
He won't be coming in today.
Just a moment.

280
00:18:03,123 --> 00:18:04,291
[WHINING]

281
00:18:04,374 --> 00:18:07,252
Auntie won't get to see Sir Eric.

282
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:09,088
[BOTH LAUGHING]

283
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:11,465
- She's sad now. [LAUGHS]
- Huh? No way!

284
00:18:11,548 --> 00:18:13,634
Cut it out! Someone might hear you.

285
00:18:13,717 --> 00:18:14,593
Too bad.

286
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:18,555
I can't believe he put me down
as his emergency contact.

287
00:18:18,639 --> 00:18:20,015
What was he expecting?

288
00:18:21,016 --> 00:18:23,560
Well, I think you did exactly
what he expected you to do.

289
00:18:24,436 --> 00:18:25,354
What?

290
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:27,314
You went to see him.

291
00:18:27,397 --> 00:18:29,066
You even paid his bill.

292
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:32,152
As if you still care.

293
00:18:34,196 --> 00:18:36,907
Dude, he listed me
as his emergency contact.

294
00:18:36,990 --> 00:18:39,785
Of course I had to pay for it. Otherwise,
the hospital might come after me later.

295
00:18:39,868 --> 00:18:41,453
[MAN] So you're Enrico's daughter?

296
00:18:41,537 --> 00:18:43,956
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

297
00:18:44,039 --> 00:18:45,207
What do you want?

298
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:48,710
Your father owes my boss
a huge sum of money.

299
00:18:48,794 --> 00:18:49,795
Over a million pesos.

300
00:18:50,587 --> 00:18:51,505
Okay.

301
00:18:51,588 --> 00:18:53,674
Okay? It isn't okay!

302
00:18:53,757 --> 00:18:55,175
He needs to pay it back.

303
00:18:55,259 --> 00:18:58,220
It's his debt, not mine.

304
00:18:58,303 --> 00:18:59,847
He doesn't have the money to pay it back.

305
00:19:00,430 --> 00:19:02,558
Then he shouldn't have borrowed
the money in the first place.

306
00:19:02,641 --> 00:19:06,395
And your boss
shouldn't have lent it to him.

307
00:19:06,478 --> 00:19:07,563
Wait a minute.

308
00:19:07,646 --> 00:19:09,148
- Hey!
- Jordan!

309
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:10,566
- That's your problem!
- Jordan!

310
00:19:10,649 --> 00:19:12,818
My friend has nothing to do with it, okay?

311
00:19:12,901 --> 00:19:14,027
- Come on, let's just go.
- Okay?!

312
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:15,320
- That's enough! Jordan!
- Let go!

313
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:20,993
We have nothing to do with his debt.
Please, leave us alone.

314
00:19:21,076 --> 00:19:22,452
Let's go.

315
00:19:22,536 --> 00:19:23,453
Let's go.

316
00:19:23,537 --> 00:19:29,585
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

317
00:19:33,505 --> 00:19:40,429
[MUSIC TURNS MOROSE]

318
00:19:42,848 --> 00:19:45,684
- [SIGHS] No…
- [PHONE RINGING]

319
00:19:45,767 --> 00:19:48,812
[PHONE RINGING]

320
00:19:51,148 --> 00:19:52,065
Hello?

321
00:19:52,149 --> 00:19:53,233
Hey.

322
00:19:53,984 --> 00:19:56,403
I just called to check if you're okay.

323
00:19:57,237 --> 00:19:58,405
I'm okay.

324
00:19:58,488 --> 00:20:00,073
Don't worry about me.

325
00:20:00,157 --> 00:20:01,241
How could I not?

326
00:20:01,825 --> 00:20:02,868
Look.

327
00:20:03,410 --> 00:20:04,912
I just thought you should know.

328
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:07,122
I'm at the police station.

329
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:09,333
What? What are you doing there?

330
00:20:09,416 --> 00:20:11,835
I don't want to add to your problems,

331
00:20:11,919 --> 00:20:15,881
but I'm sure sooner or later,
you'll find out anyway.

332
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:17,758
[JORDAN] <i>I just found out</i>

333
00:20:18,508 --> 00:20:20,177
Bea got off the hook again.

334
00:20:20,761 --> 00:20:23,597
Caloy denies that they were accomplices.

335
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:24,890
What?

336
00:20:24,973 --> 00:20:31,688
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

337
00:20:35,651 --> 00:20:37,027
<i>Bea abandoned you.</i>

338
00:20:37,110 --> 00:20:39,446
<i>Why are you still protecting her?</i>

339
00:20:39,529 --> 00:20:41,073
<i>I did it on my own.</i>

340
00:20:41,156 --> 00:20:42,658
<i>But why did you target Billy?</i>

341
00:20:43,242 --> 00:20:44,243
<i>Why?!</i>

342
00:20:44,326 --> 00:20:46,828
<i>Your father really is the worst.</i>

343
00:20:46,912 --> 00:20:48,455
<i>He even got you involved in his debts.</i>

344
00:20:48,538 --> 00:20:50,999
<i>I already knew that</i>
<i>he was only after money.</i>

345
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:52,167
<i>What if he comes back?</i>

346
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:55,379
<i>He might get the wrong idea</i>
<i>and think that you care about him.</i>

347
00:20:55,462 --> 00:20:58,215
[VALERIE] <i>You should've also mentioned</i>
<i>his partner-in-crime, Bea Mercado.</i>

348
00:20:58,298 --> 00:21:01,343
<i>And we'll let the world know</i>
<i>that she's also a criminal.</i>

349
00:21:01,426 --> 00:21:02,344
[VALERIE] <i>Yeah.</i>

350
00:21:02,427 --> 00:21:04,596
<i>Can you please talk to your people?</i>

351
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:07,599
<i>Maybe they want to know</i>
<i>what a real criminal is.</i>

352
00:21:07,683 --> 00:21:09,518
<i>Do you think you're going to scare me?</i>

353
00:21:09,601 --> 00:21:11,979
<i>Enjoy your freedom</i>
<i>because it won't last long.</i>

354
00:21:12,062 --> 00:21:13,897
<i>Ralph's mom sent this.</i>

355
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:15,482
<i>And now, they're questioning me</i>

356
00:21:15,565 --> 00:21:18,485
<i>if they did the right thing</i>
<i>when they invested in us.</i>

357
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:22,823
<i>I tried to ask</i>
<i>what the real reason is for all of this.</i>

358
00:21:22,906 --> 00:21:24,157
<i>If it's just for money.</i>

359
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:25,534
<i>It's not about money.</i>

360
00:21:25,617 --> 00:21:28,620
<i>If it were, they would've asked</i>
<i>for some a long time ago.</i>
